    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Places the nodes of a network on a 2-D (or 1-D or 3-D) map with t-SNE, so that nodes connected to the same other nodes end up close together and nodes with different connections far apart. Input: one record per connection.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Network Analysis",
    "tags": [
        "relationship",
        "analysis",
        "network",
        "graph",
        "t-sne",
        "tsne",
        "layout",
        "dimensionality reduction"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Each input record is one connection between two nodes (people, products, web pages), with an optional weight. The block describes each node by its connections (to whom, and how strongly, in either direction) and uses t-SNE to place the nodes on a map: nodes with similar connections, such as members of the same team, end up close together.\n\n**How to set it up**: choose the **From** and **To** fields and, optionally, a numeric **Weight** (such as a number of messages). Leave the other options at their defaults to start with; lower **Perplexity** for small networks (it must be at most a third of the number of nodes).\n\nThe output has one record per node: **Node**, **Dimension 1**, **Dimension 2** (and 3) and **Connections**. Plot Dimension 1 against Dimension 2 in a scatter chart. The distances between groups on a t-SNE map are not meaningful in themselves; which nodes sit together is. The same input always gives the same map.",
    "dependencies": "",
    "options": [
        {
            "name": "from",
            "title": "From field",
            "description": "One end of each connection (for example the sender).",
            "groupTitle": "Graph",
            "width": "ONE",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.FieldCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "mandatory": true,
            "inputIndex": 0,
            "defaultValue": null,
            "fieldTypes": []
        },
        {
            "name": "to",
            "title": "To field",
            "description": "The other end of each connection (for example the recipient). Connections count in both directions.",
            "groupTitle": "Graph",
            "width": "ONE",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.FieldCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "mandatory": true,
            "inputIndex": 0,
            "defaultValue": null,
            "fieldTypes": []
        },
        {
            "name": "weight",
            "title": "Weight field",
            "description": "Optional numeric field: how strong each connection is (for example a number of messages). Repeated connections between the same two nodes are added up. Without it every connection counts 1.",
            "groupTitle": "Graph",
            "width": "ONE",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.FieldCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "mandatory": false,
            "inputIndex": 0,
